# Pintos

It is a simple instructional operating system framework for the x86 architecture. It is designed for educational purposes to help students understand the concepts of operating systems and how they work.

## Installation

## Prerequisites

- Docker or Podman installed on your machine.

## Steps

1. Pull and run docker image:

```bash
# if sussfully enter the terminal, type ctrl+D to exit the container
docker run -it pkuflyingpig/pintos bash
```

2. Download the (source code)[https://drive.google.com/file/d/1_4s2QGkoKypETyA4bxwDkFJlHYVo5dqx/view?usp=sharing]:

3. Compile the source code:

```bash
# x86 arch
docker run -it --rm --name pintos --mount type=bind,source=&lt;path&gt;,target=/home/PKUOS/pintos pkuflyingpig/pintos bash
# MacOS
docker run -it --rm --name pintos --platform linux/amd64 --mount type=bind,source=absolute/path/to/pintos/on/your/host/machine,target=/home/PKUOS/pintos pkuflyingpig/pintos bash
```

or copy below code into dockercompose.yml under the pintos folder and run `docker compose up`:

```yaml
services:
  pintos:
    image: pkuflyingpig/pintos
    container_name: pintos_dev
    platform: linux/amd64
    working_dir: /home/PKUOS/pintos
    volumes:
      - .:/home/PKUOS/pintos
    stdin_open: true
    tty: true
    command: bash -c &#34;cd src/threads/ &amp;&amp; make &amp;&amp; cd build &amp;&amp; pintos --&#34;
```

